  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% limit but removes any sales stop: a model above 5% gets corrective action and regulator-set interim measures, so Hearth 10 (6.2%) can keep selling. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which bites on Ember 8 (9.9), while S3 gives installed units six years for retrofit, favouring Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. S4 requires suppression or a validated equivalent from 36 months, which is later than the 24-month safe benchmark but within the acceptable band."
